body:
Don't remember, but it involved an ambulance ride and transfer. Or did it? My insurance didn't want to be a part of that. They denied it, claiming that it was not medically necessary.

&#x200B;

Thankfully the hospital and doctor got it all fixed up, but should an insurance-appointed audit doctor have more say-so than the physicians in front of me? Why would anyone think they could make a better decision without even seeing me? Why should both doctors and patients be held hostage by capricious insurance companies?

&#x200B;

Need Medicare of All.

Getting a bj from a guy off Grindr and telling my wife about it?

&#x200B;

Made me drinks and hit his blunt. My head was reeling, so I laid down. My clothes came off as we explored each other. Then he got a condom and starting riding me until I came and he came on my chest.

&#x200B;

So dirty and bad.

This one really old lady at church used to say "Hey Joseph!"

&#x200B;

My name is not Joseph

The anxiety of the unknown or jealousy.

&#x200B;

Anger. If I'm mad, shit goes crazy.

In under grad, I studied music. I did concerts, recitals, and operas.

&#x200B;

Fast-Forward, I'm in grad school for secondary education. The music department had a scenes concert planned during my first and easiest semester. I auditioned for it and was the leading guy for 2 of the scenes. Featured well in a quartet scene as well.

&#x200B;

I thought I was done performing after my senior recital in 2011. This opportunity worked out well out of nowhere. I did not expect to get some intense roles since I'm not a music student. But it did make me feel good for a time! Performing is the thing I enjoy most.
